{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The POL-RD-01 threshold test is measured on the trace, not on the rounded trip record: gps_trace.trace_distance_km is 15.79 km against a booked optimal of 15.5 km, an excess of 0.29 km — 1.87% of the optimal route. POL-RD-01 requires the excess to exceed BOTH 0.8 km in absolute terms and 20% of optimal_distance_km; it exceeds neither. No route deviation is therefore established on this trip, and the rider's route claim fails at the gate however she characterises the trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00531", "EV-TRIP-00531"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fare is an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip: quoted_fare_sgd is 27.90 and charged_total is 27.90. Under POL-RD-11, POL-RD-02 does not run on an upfront-quoted trip and no distance-or-time refund is available to the rider however large the excess would be. The only POL-RD-11 remedy is the amount by which charged_total exceeds the quoted fare plus the properly chargeable pass-through and statutory lines — 27.90 less 27.90 — and the ledger's own computation of that remedy is 0.00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00531"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.pol_rd_11_remedy",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and must show, citing evidence IDs, an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold measured from an unimpaired trace. The trace is entirely unimpaired and yields an excess of 0.29 km, so limb (b) of that burden is not discharged. The burden never shifts to the driver, and the rider's own numerical case fails without the driver needing to invoke any exculpatory clause at all.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00531", "EV-TRIP-00531"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no billing-integrity defect to refund under POL-RD-09(4): the ledger carries no ERP gantry lines and no tolls, and airport_surcharge is 0.00, so there is no phantom gantry and no wrongly applied surcharge on this trip. The trip ORIGINATES at Changi Airport Terminal 2, so an airport surcharge is a properly chargeable pass-through under POL-RD-09 which the platform simply did not bill — which is precisely why the driver's account that the app did not cover the airport cost has a basis in the fare model rather than being an invented charge.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00531", "EV-TRIP-00531"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is complete and unimpaired for policy purposes: 133 fixes at a 10 second cadence, coverage_pct of 100.0, no gaps and a max_gap_sec of 0.0. None of POL-RD-07(a) to (c) is met — no gap over 90 seconds, no jump over 500 m, no sustained interval above 30 seconds. The case therefore does not engage the POL-RD-10(3) impairment escalation, nor the POL-RD-10(5) route, and the record is sufficient for a final monetary ruling rather than an escalation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00531"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-06 is not engaged. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 250 — a ratio of 0.00, below both the 3-flag test and the 0.05-ratio test with at least 40 completed trips. No repeat-deviation pattern is established, so no FULL_REFUND uplift under POL-RD-06(b) applies and no driver-conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c) arises on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00531"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "What the rider has formally contested is the in-app charge of SGD 27.90, which is exactly the quoted fare, and the PayNow transfer she narrates is not a line of the fare_breakdown at all — it is not a distance, time, ERP, toll or surcharge line that POL-RD-11 or POL-RD-09 can correct. The rider's own chat reply 'ok sent' confirms she was told the reason and the amount before she paid. The rider's claim is not supported by the fare record, and on NO_ACTION the present payment state — payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00 — simply stands.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00531", "EV-FARE-00531"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-RD-11"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

